CH->Could anyone give a newcomer some advice about how to identify the numerous
CH->objects found lying around in NetHack, please?  I'm VERY confused about how
Scrolls of Identify will help you quite a bit.  As will various other
methods of identification.  One that I particularly like is watch what a
monster does with something.  If it says something like

The orc quaffs the blue potion -more-
the orc suddenly looks more experienced

you know then that all blue potions are potions of gain level.  This is
only in nethack 3.1 tho..

CH->Do the colours of potions and the names of scrolls have some significance?
CH->ie, if I find a blue potion and find that (for example) it turns me
CH->invisible, can I assume that all other blue potions will do the same thing?

Only on a per game basis.  That is as long as you play that character
this will hold true but if you die and start another character then
things are randomized again.

CH->I'm not after out-and-out spoilers, but are there any files available
CH->(other than the guidebook) which give hints on how to play the game?

Keep watching this group for information on the WCST spoilers.  They are
about as spoiler as you can get but they do have a lot of useful
information in them.


